WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:02.750
- [Narrator] Let's say you're in London.

00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:04.059
You need to get from the London Eye

00:00:04.059 --> 00:00:06.220
to Buckingham Palace.

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:07.110
Taxi!

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:10.120
Buckingham Palace, please.

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:11.760
- We would leave on our
right, Belvedere Road,

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:13.830
left to Italy Street.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:16.290
- [Narrator] Wait, you know
the whole route already?

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:17.150
- Oh, we have to.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:19.960
All London black cab drivers
have to have completed

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:20.793
The Knowledge.

00:00:20.793 --> 00:00:21.659
We need to know all the streets and roads

00:00:21.659 --> 00:00:23.378
in London to provide that service.

00:00:23.378 --> 00:00:24.347
- [Narrator] All of them?

00:00:24.347 --> 00:00:27.320
Oh, okay, let's go see
where the Queen lives.

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:34.450
London is famous for its black taxis.

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:36.550
You need to get to somewhere, no sweat

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:38.550
because every black cabbie has to pass

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:39.960
an insanely hard test

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:41.900
known as The Knowledge.

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:43.550
Like this guy.

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:45.320
- Hello, my name's Peter Allen.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:46.339
I've been a London taxi driver

00:00:46.339 --> 00:00:47.878
for nine years.

00:00:47.878 --> 00:00:49.413
How can I help?

00:00:49.413 --> 00:00:51.300
The Knowledge is the test

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:52.765
that you have to pass

00:00:52.765 --> 00:00:55.250
in order to become a London taxi driver.

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:57.462
It's the toughest taxi test in the world.

00:00:57.462 --> 00:00:58.739
The first thing you have to do is

00:00:58.739 --> 00:01:01.090
learn what's called The Blue Book.

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:02.810
As a cab driver, it's your bible.

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:07.810
You have to learn 320
routes around London,

00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:10.740
so that's 640 quarter of a mile areas.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:13.408
You have to learn 25,000 streets and roads

00:01:13.408 --> 00:01:16.210
within a six-mile radius
of Trafalgar Square

00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:18.020
in London, you have to learn every single

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:19.836
point of interest, place of interest,

00:01:19.836 --> 00:01:21.970
apartment building, housing estates,

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:23.822
police stations, mosques,
synagogues, churches.

00:01:23.822 --> 00:01:26.401
- [Narrator] A few moments later.

00:01:26.401 --> 00:01:28.447
- Barber shop, furniture shop, china shop,

00:01:28.447 --> 00:01:29.986
nightclub, bars, restaurants,

00:01:29.986 --> 00:01:32.217
everything, anywhere
where a paying passenger

00:01:32.217 --> 00:01:33.175
may want to go.

00:01:33.175 --> 00:01:35.880
- [Narrator] Okay, then,
let's go the exam center.

00:01:37.998 --> 00:01:38.831
- My name is Katie Channels

00:01:38.831 --> 00:01:40.250
and I'm The Knowledge of London manager.

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:43.170
So, the exams are several phases

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:44.630
of oral appearances.

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:46.580
It's basically an interview-type situation

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:48.441
where you describe the streets and roads,

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:50.908
attempting to use the shortest distance

00:01:50.908 --> 00:01:53.280
between Point A and Point B.

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:54.390
At the beginning, we might ask them

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:56.302
the name of a theater,
where that theater is,

00:01:56.302 --> 00:01:57.830
and by the end of The Knowledge,

00:01:57.830 --> 00:01:58.765
we'd expect them to know what

00:01:58.765 --> 00:02:01.116
is actually showing at that theater.

00:02:01.116 --> 00:02:03.300
- [Narrator] On average, it takes two

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:05.080
to four years to learn The Knowledge.

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:06.810
The best way to study is to go out

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:08.424
onto the streets on a scooter.

00:02:08.424 --> 00:02:10.033
Isn't that right, Abbas?

00:02:10.033 --> 00:02:11.730
- My name is Abbas Ekta.

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:12.760
I've been studying The Knowledge

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:14.360
for about four and half years now,

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:15.320
and my next appearance is in

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:16.540
about three weeks' time.

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:17.670
It's like a full-time job.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.020
You wake up in the morning, go out

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:20.380
on a bike a couple of hours,

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:22.750
come to the college, study, study, study.

00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:24.561
Whilst I'm sleeping, I'm
studying as well, yeah.

00:02:24.561 --> 00:02:27.042
- [Narrator] One in five
who attempt The Knowledge

00:02:27.042 --> 00:02:28.129
actually pass.

00:02:28.129 --> 00:02:29.375
That's the same success rate

00:02:29.375 --> 00:02:31.218
as a U.S. Navy Seal.

00:02:31.218 --> 00:02:33.349
GPS and sat navs are banned

00:02:33.349 --> 00:02:35.780
in the exam, but why not use them

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:36.613
on the streets?

00:02:36.613 --> 00:02:37.727
- My GPS is here.

00:02:37.727 --> 00:02:39.410
And if we get somewhere and we see

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:41.105
a road's closed, we need to
say, "Right, that's closed,

00:02:41.105 --> 00:02:43.560
"but I know that if I go left here,

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:44.640
"that will take me there.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:46.180
"If I go right here,
that will take me there."

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:47.013
We need to be able to do all that

00:02:47.013 --> 00:02:48.560
as well as having a conversation

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:49.504
with the person in the back

00:02:49.504 --> 00:02:51.130
and solving the world's problems

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:52.350
at the same time.

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:53.561
- [Passenger] Leicester
Square to Big Ben, please.

00:02:53.561 --> 00:02:55.489
- So, you'd leave Leicester Square

00:02:55.489 --> 00:02:58.160
by Irving Street, turn right into

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:00.710
Charing Cross Road, go forward to --

